Rules:
  [S1] Prefer SwiftUI for new projects.
  [S2] Use MVVM architecture.
  [S3] Use Combine for reactive programming.
  [S4] Use Core Data or SwiftData for persistence.
  [S5] Use URLSession for networking.
  [S6] Use async/await for asynchronous code.
  [S7] Use Swift Package Manager for dependencies.
  [S8] Use Xcode Previews for UI development.

Pros:
  - Native performance
  - Great tooling
  - Apple ecosystem

Cons:
  - iOS only
  - App Store restrictions
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Flutter (cross-platform)
  - React Native (cross-platform)
  - Kotlin Multiplatform

State: +

